# A callee-saved register's trip through the stack is bookkeeping, and the
# listing says so in one word rather than showing the round trip: `; saves:
# RBX`. That summary is only honest if the lines it stands in for are not read
# by anything that *is* printed -- and until this rule existed they were.
#
# `push rbx ; pop rbx ; ret` printed one statement, `RBX = saved_RBX`, naming a
# variable the listing never defines. The push and the slot address it wrote
# through were elided as bookkeeping, the pop folded into the copy that lands
# the value in RBX, and what survived named the slot the dropped pair filled.
#
#   push rbx ; pop rbx ; ret
#
# The pair goes as a pair: with nothing but the pair reading what the restore
# produced, all of it goes, and the summary is the whole story.
#
# RUN: %sleigh-poc --sla=%specs/x86-64.sla --base=0 --bytes=535bc3 \
# RUN:   --passes=stack-vars,hil | FileCheck --check-prefix=ELIDED %s

# ELIDED: ; saves: RBX
# ELIDED: ; frame: retaddr[8]
# No assignment at all between the summary and the return.
# ELIDED-NOT: =
# ELIDED: return

#
#   push rbx ; mov eax, 1 ; pop rbx ; ret
#
# The same, with the instruction the function is actually about left standing
# -- and on the return line, because the value it puts in the result register
# is the function's result. What the instruction did is still there; where it
# is written is where a reader wants it.
#
# RUN: %sleigh-poc --sla=%specs/x86-64.sla --base=0 --bytes=53b8010000005bc3 \
# RUN:   --passes=stack-vars,hil | FileCheck --check-prefix=KEPT %s

# KEPT: ; saves: RBX
# KEPT-NOT: saved_RBX
# KEPT: return 0x1

#
#   push rbx ; pop rbx ; mov [rdi], rbx ; ret
#
# The other side of the rule. Something outside the pair reads the register the
# restore produced, so the restore is work the program does and none of the
# group is elided -- not the copy, not the load, and not the address, because
# `&saved_RBX = RSP - 0x8` is the line that defines the name the two of them are
# written with. A listing may show a slot, or summarise it, but never half of
# each.
#
# RUN: %sleigh-poc --sla=%specs/x86-64.sla --base=0 --bytes=535b48891fc3 \
# RUN:   --passes=stack-vars,hil | FileCheck --check-prefix=SHOWN %s

# SHOWN: ; saves: RBX
# SHOWN: &saved_RBX#1 = RSP#in - 0x8
# SHOWN: saved_RBX#1 = RBX#in
# SHOWN: RBX#1 = saved_RBX#1
# SHOWN: [RDI] = RBX#1
